From 7ee45702d605efe4e4fbf18ac98a496cddd2abf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:17:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 840/913] dts: stm32: set i2c4 as secure and control PMIC on
 stm32mp15xx-dkx boards

On boards stm32mp15xx-dkx:
In order to secure i2c4, move the control of STPMIC from Linux to OP-TEE
and expose corresponding regulators thru SCMI.

Also change LPTIM4 source clock to LSI, required by PSCI-OSI feature.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 14b12a21d4d819695a53054b3317b543a14db092 dts: stm32: set i2c4 as secure and control PMIC on stm32mp15xx-dkx boards]
